## Summary

Implemented issue #32: added OKF v0.2 `type` frontmatter across all 65 non-exempt Markdown/MDX files under `docs/**` and `src/content/docs/**`, derived mechanically from existing `kind` (Diataxis) or a documented folder-path vocabulary (Fumadocs site content), plus `status: draft` on site content. Built `scripts/validate-okf.ts` as the single conformance seam with a `node:test`-based unit test suite (14 tests, no new dependency, reusing `docs-discovery`'s hand-rolled frontmatter-parsing approach), wired into new `pnpm test`/`pnpm validate:okf` scripts and a separate CI job. Documented the `kind→type` and site-content `type` vocabulary tables in `docs/agents/domain.md`. `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`, `pnpm exec eslint .`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm validate:okf` all pass clean against the live repo. A two-axis code review (Standards + Spec) surfaced one real gap — the new test file wasn't wired into any run path — which I fixed by adding `pnpm test` and a CI step; the remaining minor duplication with `discover.ts` was left alone since touching that shared skill file is explicitly out of scope. Work is committed on `feat/32-okf-frontmatter`.

One judgment call worth a human's attention: I exempted root `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` from the `type` requirement (documented in code and in `domain.md`), reasoning they're loaded verbatim as runtime agent instructions like `SKILL.md`, unlike `docs/agents/*.md` which only get read via `docs-discovery` tooling. The issue never explicitly addresses these two files either way, so this is a reasonable but not spec-mandated interpretation — flagged in the commit message for review.

